  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AZS4-QA-008" ;
  triage:title "next_ephemeral's run_blocking call remains unbounded after partial hardening fix (RSH-001)" ;
  triage:description "Reported by quality-mgr's formal QA-1 verdict for AZ.4 (PR #1387) as RSH-001, described as a partial fix: rust-service-hardening-agent's earlier finding about unbounded spawn_blocking usage was fixed for most call sites in this sprint's diff, but crates/atm-http-runtime/src/herdr_attention_scheduler.rs's next_ephemeral function (around line 102-114 in the version at pinned head 7f5df3bfdb90d16dd4fbde2a6e563bac7bba084d) still calls run_blocking without a timeout/deadline bound, unlike reserve_next_attention and next_persistent_task which use ReadDeadline/SCHEDULER_REQUEST_DEADLINE. Confirmed by quality-mgr's rust-service-hardening-agent reviewer at pinned head 7f5df3bfdb90d16dd4fbde2a6e563bac7bba084d via git show." ;
